## Pillar 1 — extend test coverage to the UI and the sync refresh path

Context: follow-up to the section above. The first pass covered the backend well
but left three gaps: the frontend had no coverage at all (both confirmation
dialogs and all three drift surfaces), the synchronous
`Domain.update_metadata_tables` diff was written but never exercised, and the
two new routes were only reached by e2e tests running against an empty session,
where every interesting assertion is vacuously true. No production code changed.

The frontend tests follow the existing repo convention (`tests/units/front/`):
Python contract tests that parse the JS source and assert on structure, since
there is no JS test runner. They were mutation-checked — inverting the save gate
in `monitorMetadataTask` and flipping the drift badge from `bg-warning` to
`bg-danger` each failed the expected tests, then were reverted.

Changes:

1. tests/units/front/test_metadata_guard_ui.py
   New — 31 cases. Deletion guard: the pre-flight hits
   `/domain/metadata/removal-impact`, skips the round-trip for an empty
   selection, and degrades to the plain confirm on error rather than making the
   removal impossible; the escalated dialog carries the danger header, the
   dedup'd mapping count and the R2RML warning; both call sites pass the right
   identifiers, honour cancel, and confirm *before* issuing the destructive
   request. Diff preview: every change kind renders, removals are listed first,
   unchanged columns are summarised not enumerated, and both builders escape
   table/column names. The save gate gets its own class asserting an empty diff
   saves without prompting, declining breaks out before the save call and
   reloads the stored state, and confirming still persists. Also covers the new
   `detailHtml`/`size`/`headerClass` options on `showConfirmDialog`, including
   that their defaults leave existing callers' markup unchanged.
2. tests/units/front/test_schema_drift_ui.py
   New — 28 cases. The fetch uses the cheap `/mapping/schema-drift` route (not
   `/diagnostics`), runs in parallel with the map layout, and cannot throw. The
   canvas marker only renders on affected nodes, does not replace the mapping
   status ring, and names the missing columns in the tooltip. Both panel banners
   use `alert-warning` rather than `alert-danger` — drift is advisory — and the
   column-header badge appends to rather than overwrites the existing ID/Label/
   attribute badge. Diagnostics: drift rows get their own icon and a stripped,
   annotated label; the header badge counts them, hides when clean, appears on
   entities and relationships alike, and reads as a warning.
3. tests/units/api/test_integrity_endpoints.py
   New — 9 cases hitting both routes through `TestClient`. Covers what the e2e
   suite structurally cannot: a session that actually has mappings (patched at
   the service layer), the dedup'd `affected_mapping_count`, a missing
   `table_names` key, that the impact route mutates nothing, and that
   `/mapping/schema-drift` never falls through to `run_diagnostics`.
4. tests/units/domain/test_metadata_refresh_diff.py
   New `TestSyncUpdateDiff` (4 cases) covering the previously untested
   synchronous `Domain.update_metadata_tables`: added/removed columns, type
   changes, a clean refresh producing an empty diff, and that — unlike the async
   task — this path does persist, since there is no browser round-trip after it
   to gate. Note for future readers: `back.objects.domain.Domain` resolves to
   the re-exported *class*, so the module-level names have to be patched via
   `sys.modules`. Also added a case asserting one table failing its `DESCRIBE`
   does not discard the diffs computed for its siblings.
5. tests/units/domain/test_metadata_removal_guard.py
   New `TestTablesWithoutFullName` (4 cases) — legacy metadata rows carry only
   `name`, and the guard must still match them on both the save and clear paths
   — and `TestSqlOnlyReferenceIsGuarded` (1 case) asserting a table referenced
   only from a mapping's freeform SQL still triggers invalidation.

